Bootstrap is a CSS framework. It is used to create very effective UI designs easily. 
It provides pre-built components like buttons, nav-bars, carousels, etc. We can add these components in our projects by adding their pre-written html codes.
We can use the pre-defined classes provided by Bootstrap, add them to our components so that they will automatically get styled without us writting any CSS.

Befits:
i) Helps creating complex frontend quickly.
ii) No need to worry about CSS properties. 
iii) It is fast an reliable as the CSS is provided via CDN. 

Disadavantages:
i) Makes the HTML file bloated with classes, which makes the code hard to read.
ii) Does not follows separation of concerns. HTML file should be used for structure not for styling.
iii) It could not be used to create custom designs. We have to use the pre-built designs provided by Bootstrap.

How to use?
i) Go to getbootstrap.com
ii) copy the CDN link to the head section of html and copy the script link at the bottom of body (before closing tag).
iii) go to docs section of bootstrap, look for the component required and add its code to your file.
